---
import LegalLayout from "../layouts/LegalLayout.astro";
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Privacy Policy • Volynx"
  description="Volynx privacy policy: what we collect, why, and how you control your data."
>
  <div class="kicker">Legal</div>
  <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
  <p>This policy explains how Volynx collects, uses, and protects personal data. Replace/expand sections to match your actual stack (forms, analytics, payments).</p>

  <h2>What we collect</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Contact data</strong> (e.g., name, email) when you submit forms or request support.</li>
    <li><strong>Usage data</strong> (e.g., pages visited, device/browser) when analytics are enabled.</li>
    <li><strong>Transaction data</strong> if you purchase products (handled by the payment provider).</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Why we collect it</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>To deliver products and respond to requests</li>
    <li>To improve performance and user experience</li>
    <li>To meet legal and security obligations</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Cookies</h2>
  <p>We may use cookies for essential functionality and analytics. If you have a dedicated Cookies Policy page, link it here.</p>

  <h2>Your choices</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Request access, correction, or deletion of your data</li>
    <li>Opt out of marketing emails at any time</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>Privacy requests: <a href="mailto:privacy@volynx.world">privacy@volynx.world</a> (or use your main email).</p>
  <p class="meta">Last updated: {new Date().toISOString().slice(0, 10)}</p>
</LegalLayout>
